figdown 0.1 bitfield
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: `step` is RESERVED inside an index= range. `INDEX-RANGE-STEP` filed
# `index="0..7 step 2"` as a v0.2 extension needing "no new key and no
# migration" — but a prose <last> accepted any non-empty text, so that
# spelling was already a LEGAL document with the model {first:0,
# last:"7 step 2"}. Shipping the meaning later would have changed what an
# existing document MEANS, and no engine could separate prose that reads like
# a step clause from an author who meant the extension: the `color=` failure
# shape. An extension is free only when its syntax is RESERVED, not merely
# unused. The trigger is a BARE lowercase `step` token in the prose <last>.
bitfield b "Header" numbering=msb0
field "Base" 8
field "S" 8 index="0..7 step 2"
field "T" 8 index="0..N step 2"
field "U" 8 index="0..end step"
